        <item>
            <title>0.6.20</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:56:36 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:channel>beta</sparkle:channel>
            <sparkle:version>149</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.6.20</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### New
- **Chat view for P‍i.** Run a P‍i session as a native chat instead of the terminal: pick Terminal or Chat in the preparation sheet, or switch from the workspace header. The same session continues in the other view.
- **Chat composer.** Return sends, Shift+Return adds a line, Escape stops the run. Attach files with the plus button, by dropping them, or by pasting an image. Type `/` for the commands your P‍i extensions and skills provide. Pick the model and thinking level from the composer.
- **Readable timeline.** Replies render Markdown with lists, headings and code blocks you can copy. Thinking and tool calls fold under a "Worked for" line; two buttons in the corner show or hide them.
- **List view.** Settings > General > Project view, or the toolbar switch, shows every session of a project in one list instead of the board. New Session goes straight to the preparation sheet.
- **P‍i can be switched off.** Settings > P‍i Runtime > Enabled. If you only use Claude Code or O‍penCode, the board no longer asks you to install P‍i.
- The chat shows which P‍i agent is active and the status text of your extensions.

### Changed
- New tasks use the first enabled agent when the project's default agent is switched off.
- Duplicating a task keeps its agent.

### Fixed
- A "Resume Anyway" banner from one task no longer stays on screen after opening another task, and that task now resumes on its own.
]]></description>
